(2665135, 366006, 24454, '<td valign="top">Charmayne, this is breathtaking!   I didn''t get to finish voting on this challenge so I missed this one, but I would have given it a 10 (don''t you hate hearing stuff like that after a challenge when the 10 could have helped so much. . .darn).   But really:  in a challenge like this with so many stunning works of art, this one had an impressively strong finish!!!!  <br/> <br/>Exceptional work!!!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Charmayne, this is breathtaking!   I didn''t get to finish voting on this challenge so I missed this one, but I would have given it a 10 (don''t you hate hearing stuff like that after a challenge when the 10 could have helped so much. . .darn).   But really:  in a challenge like this with so many stunning works of art, this one had an impressively strong finish!!!!   Exceptional work!!! ', '2006-07-26 19:26:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2665144, 365897, 27373, '<td valign="top">First let me say I would''ve given you a "1" here''s why<br/> <br/>1) They didn''t have M-16''s in WWII<br/>2) A couple of these guys look British- one appears to be carrying an SA80- also not around in World War II.<br/>3) The sand is clearly out of scale with the rest of the image<br/>4) Ever since Toy Story I get the willies just seeing these guys<br/>5) The helmet for the guy on the left is just all wrong, wrong wrong wrong!<br/> <br/>Okay, so now you''re saying- what a D***.  In reality I like the shot, it clearly took some planning and thought.  I like the shallow DOF adds to the illusion.  I probably would have given you a 7 just for making me laugh and then a bonus of 1 for coming up with the idea, so an 8.  Hopefully when you read #4 you picked up on the joke before calling me names.  Keep shooting and having fun with it.  DPC needs more out of the box thinkers- in fact everywhere does.<br/> <br/></td>', 'First let me say I would''ve given you a "1" here''s why 1) They didn''t have M-16''s in WWII2) A couple of these guys look British- one appears to be carrying an SA80- also not around in World War II.3) The sand is clearly out of scale with the rest of the image4) Ever since Toy Story I get the willies just seeing these guys5) The helmet for the guy on the left is just all wrong, wrong wrong wrong! Okay, so now you''re saying- what a D***.  In reality I like the shot, it clearly took some planning and thought.  I like the shallow DOF adds to the illusion.  I probably would have given you a 7 just for making me laugh and then a bonus of 1 for coming up with the idea, so an 8.  Hopefully when you read #4 you picked up on the joke before calling me names.  Keep shooting and having fun with it.  DPC needs more out of the box thinkers- in fact everywhere does. ', '2006-07-26 19:27:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(2665154, 363533, 24454, '<td valign="top">This is way wayyyyyyyyy underrated!   It''s beautiful!   You did really good!!!!!!   Way to go showing that we have beautiful scenery here too!<br/> <br/></td>', 'This is way wayyyyyyyyy underrated!   It''s beautiful!   You did really good!!!!!!   Way to go showing that we have beautiful scenery here too! ', '2006-07-26 19:29:30.000000', NULL, 0),
