(2682360, 364540, 22301, '<td valign="top">Joshua, thanks for your comment on my on the beach entry and I thoght I would return the comment. This is a cool shot I love the fallen trees and I went to school in San Luis Obispo so its nice to see something taken close to there. I really like like your attempt to match the smoothness of the water to the tree. But my tow things I might try to change would be to be closer to the tree since it is alittle hard to see how smooth the tree is. The second is that the photo appears alittle cool and wish the photo had more tints of red and magentas. That is only my opinion though and you can take it if you would like. THanks again for your comment and way to have such a high finish.<br/>joe</td>', 'Joshua, thanks for your comment on my on the beach entry and I thoght I would return the comment. This is a cool shot I love the fallen trees and I went to school in San Luis Obispo so its nice to see something taken close to there. I really like like your attempt to match the smoothness of the water to the tree. But my tow things I might try to change would be to be closer to the tree since it is alittle hard to see how smooth the tree is. The second is that the photo appears alittle cool and wish the photo had more tints of red and magentas. That is only my opinion though and you can take it if you would like. THanks again for your comment and way to have such a high finish.joe', '2006-08-01 00:53:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(2682370, 363474, 22301, '<td valign="top">Thomas, thanks for your comment on my on the beach entry and thought I would give you a comment back. This is a great shot and congrats on your top ten finish. Hard to find too much to critique on this imagem the only thing I would have like to seen is the foreground be a bit brighter, but thats just personal taste. THanks for your comment again and this is a really nice shot.<br/>joe</td>', 'Thomas, thanks for your comment on my on the beach entry and thought I would give you a comment back. This is a great shot and congrats on your top ten finish. Hard to find too much to critique on this imagem the only thing I would have like to seen is the foreground be a bit brighter, but thats just personal taste. THanks for your comment again and this is a really nice shot.joe', '2006-08-01 01:01:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(2682389, 365889, 12448, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/>Okay, no offense but I seem to keep pulling the ribbon shots, LOL  There is nothing wrong with this shot, LOL<br/> <br/>Okay, I''ll be serious now.<br/> <br/>I love this shot, it''s calm, peaceful and you would, without a doubt find it on a beach.  The exposure time on this is perfect and looking at your outtakes, you choose well.<br/> <br/>I really can''t find anything wrong with this shot, it''s beautiful.  I''m sorry, I wish I could offer more!<br/> <br/>I hope my comments help and Good Luck in future Challenges!<br/> <br/>Deannda</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club. Okay, no offense but I seem to keep pulling the ribbon shots, LOL  There is nothing wrong with this shot, LOL Okay, I''ll be serious now. I love this shot, it''s calm, peaceful and you would, without a doubt find it on a beach.  The exposure time on this is perfect and looking at your outtakes, you choose well. I really can''t find anything wrong with this shot, it''s beautiful.  I''m sorry, I wish I could offer more! I hope my comments help and Good Luck in future Challenges! Deannda', '2006-08-01 01:12:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2682402, 364081, 20168, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all your vote and comments! I''ve been away hiking this past week, and came home to find "Low Tide" among the DPC ribbons! A delight to place among the ribbon winners, especially on my 50th entry.</td>', 'Thanks for all your vote and comments! I''ve been away hiking this past week, and came home to find "Low Tide" among the DPC ribbons! A delight to place among the ribbon winners, especially on my 50th entry.', '2006-08-01 01:22:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(2682411, 365939, 22301, '<td valign="top">Jim, Thanks for your comment on my beach entry I thought I would return the favor.  Congratulations on your sixth place finish, the exposure on this photo is spot on and way to hide the freighter, not easy to hide such a massive boat, lol. I just wanted say congrats and welcome to the 7+ score no ribbon club. Thanks again for your comment.<br/>joe</td>', 'Jim, Thanks for your comment on my beach entry I thought I would return the favor.  Congratulations on your sixth place finish, the exposure on this photo is spot on and way to hide the freighter, not easy to hide such a massive boat, lol. I just wanted say congrats and welcome to the 7+ score no ribbon club. Thanks again for your comment.joe', '2006-08-01 01:25:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(2682458, 365537, 63135, '<td valign="top">Very Nice photo, Perfect timing</td>', 'Very Nice photo, Perfect timing', '2006-08-01 01:43:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(2682469, 364270, 52731, '<td valign="top">Wow, what a beautiful and interesting little guy you''ve found here. I really like that deep purple red color you''ve captured, and think this has a nice composition to it. I do think that it is a bit oversharpened, but nonetheless a good photo.<br/> <br/>Keep up the good work!<br/> <br/>-Monica</td>', 'Wow, what a beautiful and interesting little guy you''ve found here. I really like that deep purple red color you''ve captured, and think this has a nice composition to it. I do think that it is a bit oversharpened, but nonetheless a good photo. Keep up the good work! -Monica', '2006-08-01 01:46:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(2682482, 365119, 22301, '<td valign="top">john, thanks for the comment and I thoughtI would return the comment. This is a nice shot of the water but the colors and greens feel oversaturated.  I think as suggested havin someone else in the photo may have helped also. I really like how you have the reeds in bottom  left, its a nice detail. Thanks again for your comment. joe</td>', 'john, thanks for the comment and I thoughtI would return the comment. This is a nice shot of the water but the colors and greens feel oversaturated.  I think as suggested havin someone else in the photo may have helped also. I really like how you have the reeds in bottom  left, its a nice detail. Thanks again for your comment. joe', '2006-08-01 01:50:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(2682521, 365427, 60805, '<td valign="top">Your comments helped me plenty. I got tunnel vision on the driftwood, not paying attention to the horizon. But u live n learn. I really find it difficult working with lighting and its going to take a lot of practice. Trying to find the sweet spot with a 1/2.5 CCD is very challenging. But it''ll have to do until i go APS-C or full SLR.<br/>And with u guys steering me n the right direction, i''ll iron out the bugs soon enuff. So thanks again for u''r constructive criticism, it means a lot to me. Keep it coming hard I can take it.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Neuferland:</b></div><hr/><i> Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Why yes, I can see the Barracuda! ;)  Very nice.<br/> <br/>This is a good shot and with a little work could be a fantastic shot.  I like the composition and the idea behind the shot.  Nice eye catching the image in the driftwood.<br/> <br/>But two things caught my eye almost immediately, first the feel of the shot, working in the direct sun can be a nightmare and this is one of those instances.  Looking up your camera I see you can adjust the aperture settings and when working with bright light like this you might want to close your aperture just another notch or two.  Make it a little darker and work with it later in Photoshop if you need.  Or even try a couple of different settings to see how they come out.  The hardest thing to learn with a camera is lighting.  I''m still fighting with mine most of the time.<br/> <br/>Next was the horizon, even though you did a great job with your DOF, you kept my attention on the wood and still had enough detail to the ocean to make it a viable part of the picture, the horizon is very crooked.  A problem in that it throws the whole shot off but how would the driftwood look if you tilted it to correct the ocean? Well, using my magic envelopes, I took off the bottom of the picture and the peice of wood right behind the Barracuda so all I could see was the ocean and the part of the driftwood that is the Barracuda.  What a difference this made in the shot. I didn''t have all this other stuff fighting for my attention and the wood really stands out against the ocean, making one think the barracuda was jumping from the ocean.  Maybe if you were a little lower and reframed your shot?  And watch your horizon.<br/> <br/>One last thing, the title.  BARRACUDA!!  would have been plenty.  If you can use less words, do ;)<br/> <br/>Well, looking at your profile, this is your 4th challenge, let me say Welcome to DPChallenge and keep it up, I really like your ship shot.<br/> <br/>I hope my comments help and Good Luck in future Challenges!<br/> <br/>Deannda </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Your comments helped me plenty. I got tunnel vision on the driftwood, not paying attention to the horizon. But u live n learn. I really find it difficult working with lighting and its going to take a lot of practice. Trying to find the sweet spot with a 1/2.5 CCD is very challenging. But it''ll have to do until i go APS-C or full SLR.And with u guys steering me n the right direction, i''ll iron out the bugs soon enuff. So thanks again for u''r constructive criticism, it means a lot to me. Keep it coming hard I can take it. Originally posted by Neuferland: Greetings from the Critique Club! Why yes, I can see the Barracuda! ;)  Very nice. This is a good shot and with a little work could be a fantastic shot.  I like the composition and the idea behind the shot.  Nice eye catching the image in the driftwood. But two things caught my eye almost immediately, first the feel of the shot, working in the direct sun can be a nightmare and this is one of those instances.  Looking up your camera I see you can adjust the aperture settings and when working with bright light like this you might want to close your aperture just another notch or two.  Make it a little darker and work with it later in Photoshop if you need.  Or even try a couple of different settings to see how they come out.  The hardest thing to learn with a camera is lighting.  I''m still fighting with mine most of the time. Next was the horizon, even though you did a great job with your DOF, you kept my attention on the wood and still had enough detail to the ocean to make it a viable part of the picture, the horizon is very crooked.  A problem in that it throws the whole shot off but how would the driftwood look if you tilted it to correct the ocean? Well, using my magic envelopes, I took off the bottom of the picture and the peice of wood right behind the Barracuda so all I could see was the ocean and the part of the driftwood that is the Barracuda.  What a difference this made in the shot. I didn''t have all this other stuff fighting for my attention and the wood really stands out against the ocean, making one think the barracuda was jumping from the ocean.  Maybe if you were a little lower and reframed your shot?  And watch your horizon. One last thing, the title.  BARRACUDA!!  would have been plenty.  If you can use less words, do ;) Well, looking at your profile, this is your 4th challenge, let me say Welcome to DPChallenge and keep it up, I really like your ship shot. I hope my comments help and Good Luck in future Challenges! Deannda ', '2006-08-01 02:01:21.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(2682533, 366114, 22301, '<td valign="top">Thanks for your comment on my beach entry I thoguth I would give you a comment back. I thought this entry was really good, I really like the reflections in the water both from the hill and from your son moving around. The only critique would be I could think of is that I wish your son was more in focus and the photo was just alittle brighter, just my opinioin though. THanks again for the comment.<br/>joe</td>', 'Thanks for your comment on my beach entry I thoguth I would give you a comment back. I thought this entry was really good, I really like the reflections in the water both from the hill and from your son moving around. The only critique would be I could think of is that I wish your son was more in focus and the photo was just alittle brighter, just my opinioin though. THanks again for the comment.joe', '2006-08-01 02:04:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(2682553, 366073, 22301, '<td valign="top">Alison, thanks for your comment on my beach entry I thoguth I would give you a comment too.  i think it is too hard to see what is going on and you will get better score with straight horizon and larger photos. Here is the link to the <a href="//dpchallenge.com/tutorial.php?TUTORIAL_ID=26" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">tutorial</a> mentioned in your comments during the challenge. Thanks again for your comment.<br/>joe</td>', 'Alison, thanks for your comment on my beach entry I thoguth I would give you a comment too.  i think it is too hard to see what is going on and you will get better score with straight horizon and larger photos. Here is the link to the tutorial mentioned in your comments during the challenge. Thanks again for your comment.joe', '2006-08-01 02:11:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2682596, 365174, 22301, '<td valign="top">Dave,<br/> thanks for your comment on my beach entry and I would give a comment back. The first thing I looked at was your file size and that it was 84 kb and thought you might want to see this <a href="//dpchallenge.com/tutorial.php?TUTORIAL_ID=26" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">tutorial</a> for photoshop on how to prepare image for submission. Your small details would much smoother if your file size was closer to the 150 kb size limit. I really think it is a cool way that you shot the photo too! I appreciate your comment, thanks again.<br/>joe</td>', 'Dave, thanks for your comment on my beach entry and I would give a comment back. The first thing I looked at was your file size and that it was 84 kb and thought you might want to see this tutorial for photoshop on how to prepare image for submission. Your small details would much smoother if your file size was closer to the 150 kb size limit. I really think it is a cool way that you shot the photo too! I appreciate your comment, thanks again.joe', '2006-08-01 02:51:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(2682675, 365919, 22301, '<td valign="top">Linda, <br/>Thanks for your comment on my Beach entry, i thought I would give you a comment back. The color and lines are nice and done well and I like the angle. The problem I could see from voters perspective is that you  have no beach in your shot, just sand and the challenge was really to shoot by the water, not a beach, so I had scored this a five and I think alot of others may have thought the same and voted similarly. Hope that helps, thanks again.<br/>joe</td>', 'Linda, Thanks for your comment on my Beach entry, i thought I would give you a comment back. The color and lines are nice and done well and I like the angle. The problem I could see from voters perspective is that you  have no beach in your shot, just sand and the challenge was really to shoot by the water, not a beach, so I had scored this a five and I think alot of others may have thought the same and voted similarly. Hope that helps, thanks again.joe', '2006-08-01 03:08:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2682735, 365703, 22301, '<td valign="top">Hey this looks familiar!! ALice, i had a great time at the GTG on sat. I am giving everyone a comment/critique who commented onmy image for the beach on the challenge and this is my 57th, yowsahs.  I really like your shot and during the cahllenge I gave it a 7. One thing I would like to have seen was the end of the bridge on the right so it feels abit more complete. Other than that yours is great and has much more realistic colors then my entry. I actually have on shot from nearly this same spot at night, with the reflection in the sand. My shot was about two rocks over. Luckily the nudies were all gone when I got there. Thanks again for your comment. <br/>Joe</td>', 'Hey this looks familiar!! ALice, i had a great time at the GTG on sat. I am giving everyone a comment/critique who commented onmy image for the beach on the challenge and this is my 57th, yowsahs.  I really like your shot and during the cahllenge I gave it a 7. One thing I would like to have seen was the end of the bridge on the right so it feels abit more complete. Other than that yours is great and has much more realistic colors then my entry. I actually have on shot from nearly this same spot at night, with the reflection in the sand. My shot was about two rocks over. Luckily the nudies were all gone when I got there. Thanks again for your comment. Joe', '2006-08-01 03:26:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(2682742, 366195, 22301, '<td valign="top">Hey jen, I am giving a comment to everyone who gave me one for the beach challenge and your the last one! So I apologize if its not too good, Lol. First thing I noticed was the horizon is abit tilted.  i think I may have tried to  move the horizon up or down because I knida feel it cuttin the photo in two. I really like the dpeth of field and sepia toning in the photo. Congrats on the fav, now lets go F-stops!!<br/>Joe</td>', 'Hey jen, I am giving a comment to everyone who gave me one for the beach challenge and your the last one! So I apologize if its not too good, Lol. First thing I noticed was the horizon is abit tilted.  i think I may have tried to  move the horizon up or down because I knida feel it cuttin the photo in two. I really like the dpeth of field and sepia toning in the photo. Congrats on the fav, now lets go F-stops!!Joe', '2006-08-01 03:32:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(2682827, 362719, 9668, '<td valign="top">Bummer on the DQ! Awesome image though.</td>', 'Bummer on the DQ! Awesome image though.', '2006-08-01 04:40:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(2682867, 366215, 21816, '<td valign="top"><b>* Greetings from the Critique Club *</b> <br/> <br/>Hi Gerry. What a nice candid capture you have taken here. It''s definately a nice beach silhouette shot and the golden colour reflecting off the water indicates late afternoon.<br/> <br/>The main thing that bothers me about this photo is where the ''brother'' is positioned in relation to the frame. It''s very hard to tell if you could of used another crop without seeing the original photo but I find that he''s just too close to the edge of the frame. Someone even mentioned cropping him out altogether. That was another possibility perhaps?<br/> <br/>You''ve used a nice depth of field to keep the water nicely in focus across the whole photo which has worked well. As I mentioned earlier, the colour of the sun reflecting on the water is fantastic.<br/> <br/>It''s always hard to say why a photo scores what it does. I''ve always believed that a photo gets voted what the people think it deserves. You''ve done well with this shot and should be proud of it. Best of luck with your future challenges!<br/> <br/>Neil</td>', '* Greetings from the Critique Club *  Hi Gerry. What a nice candid capture you have taken here. It''s definately a nice beach silhouette shot and the golden colour reflecting off the water indicates late afternoon. The main thing that bothers me about this photo is where the ''brother'' is positioned in relation to the frame. It''s very hard to tell if you could of used another crop without seeing the original photo but I find that he''s just too close to the edge of the frame. Someone even mentioned cropping him out altogether. That was another possibility perhaps? You''ve used a nice depth of field to keep the water nicely in focus across the whole photo which has worked well. As I mentioned earlier, the colour of the sun reflecting on the water is fantastic. It''s always hard to say why a photo scores what it does. I''ve always believed that a photo gets voted what the people think it deserves. You''ve done well with this shot and should be proud of it. Best of luck with your future challenges! Neil', '2006-08-01 05:41:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(2683164, 365801, 21816, '<td valign="top"><b>* Greetings from the Critique Club *</b> <br/> <br/>Hi Arnthor. Looks like the voters were relatively happy with this photo but there were a few with criticisms amonst the comments. <br/> <br/>It is to me a photo of two halves. With the fill flash fired out front it makes the lower half seem like night time whilst the waves and the hillside indicate early morning in the top half. It just doesn''t seem balanced in that regard. Maybe you could of cut the flash back a stop? <br/> <br/>The scene itself I think is fantastic but the horizon is leaning to the right. The patterns in the sand and the water along the shore add a lot of character to the shot. You''ve used a nice depth of field to keep the focus throughout the photo and it looks crisp and sharp.<br/> <br/>Overall you did a nice job on this but the horizon, as I have learnt, will always get criticised if it''s slightly skewiff and will cost votes. You''ve got some amazing photos in your portfolio and even though this finished below your average it''s still a great effort. Well done and best of luck with future challenges.<br/> <br/>Neil</td>', '* Greetings from the Critique Club *  Hi Arnthor. Looks like the voters were relatively happy with this photo but there were a few with criticisms amonst the comments.  It is to me a photo of two halves. With the fill flash fired out front it makes the lower half seem like night time whilst the waves and the hillside indicate early morning in the top half. It just doesn''t seem balanced in that regard. Maybe you could of cut the flash back a stop?  The scene itself I think is fantastic but the horizon is leaning to the right. The patterns in the sand and the water along the shore add a lot of character to the shot. You''ve used a nice depth of field to keep the focus throughout the photo and it looks crisp and sharp. Overall you did a nice job on this but the horizon, as I have learnt, will always get criticised if it''s slightly skewiff and will cost votes. You''ve got some amazing photos in your portfolio and even though this finished below your average it''s still a great effort. Well done and best of luck with future challenges. Neil', '2006-08-01 09:35:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2683529, 365493, 27922, '<td valign="top">Alright, A lot of very interesting comments on this one. I am always the person saying "who is going to be the Jack a-- that has a naked girl on this competition?" Well... It was me this time. I have been gone for a while and only put this shot in because it was what I had and was excited to enter in a DPC comp. <br/> <br/>-Thank everyone for your comments. I will work on better shots for next time.</td>', 'Alright, A lot of very interesting comments on this one. I am always the person saying "who is going to be the Jack a-- that has a naked girl on this competition?" Well... It was me this time. I have been gone for a while and only put this shot in because it was what I had and was excited to enter in a DPC comp.  -Thank everyone for your comments. I will work on better shots for next time.', '2006-08-01 12:15:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(2683688, 365810, 20168, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the ribbon and thanks for a beautiful image!</td>', 'Congrats on the ribbon and thanks for a beautiful image!', '2006-08-01 13:33:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(2683709, 365889, 20168, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your ribbon and bringing to the DPC community a lovely image of the old wooden boat way of life which was so common 100 years ago!</td>', 'Congrats on your ribbon and bringing to the DPC community a lovely image of the old wooden boat way of life which was so common 100 years ago!', '2006-08-01 13:39:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(2684545, 364994, 7889, '<td valign="top">Yeh this is sooo good! Well done on your 4 place, there were some outstanding photos in this challenge.<br/> <br/>Mike<br/> <br/></td>', 'Yeh this is sooo good! Well done on your 4 place, there were some outstanding photos in this challenge. Mike ', '2006-08-01 18:09:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2684645, 366114, 34938, '<td valign="top">This was one of the most underrated shots in this challenge...by a long shot...congrats on a great photo Ragga</td>', 'This was one of the most underrated shots in this challenge...by a long shot...congrats on a great photo Ragga', '2006-08-01 18:37:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(2684653, 364293, 34938, '<td valign="top">This was worth more than 105th! Sad to see you were robbed of votes here...91 x 6''s is good though</td>', 'This was worth more than 105th! Sad to see you were robbed of votes here...91 x 6''s is good though', '2006-08-01 18:39:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(2684831, 365821, 14476, '<td valign="top">Good Grief!  As as big fan of Nevil Shute''s work, and even with the huge hint in your title, I never made the connection.  Not how I thought of the setting for his Down Under, extremely compelling novel.<br/> <br/>Glad to have another chance to look at this image.<br/> <br/>Alice</td>', 'Good Grief!  As as big fan of Nevil Shute''s work, and even with the huge hint in your title, I never made the connection.  Not how I thought of the setting for his Down Under, extremely compelling novel. Glad to have another chance to look at this image. Alice', '2006-08-01 19:24:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(2685316, 365944, 44441, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by graphicfunk:</b></div><hr/><i> Like a trip into the mystic! Congratulations on your top 20 finish. </i></td></tr></table>Thank you! It is actually the Tulum ruins, not Uxmal; oops! :)</td>', 'Originally posted by graphicfunk: Like a trip into the mystic! Congratulations on your top 20 finish. Thank you! It is actually the Tulum ruins, not Uxmal; oops! :)', '2006-08-01 21:49:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(2685913, 365939, 12448, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Wow, what a shot!!! Very nice indeed!<br/> <br/>You are right about those palm leaves though, a bit of a distraction but not much.  Being a basic challenge you were very limited in that department.  About the only other thing I noticed when looking at it is the bump behind the tree right at the horizon line.  Is that a rock or island?  Again, not much you could do because of the type of challenge.  But that is honestly about all I could find wrong with the shot.<br/> <br/>Love your profile shot, very cute.  And looking at your other pictures this was a very nice challenge for you!  You have a good eye for this and I can''t wait to see you rise in the ranks here.<br/> <br/>I hope my comments help and good luck in Future Challenges!<br/> <br/>Deannda</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Wow, what a shot!!! Very nice indeed! You are right about those palm leaves though, a bit of a distraction but not much.  Being a basic challenge you were very limited in that department.  About the only other thing I noticed when looking at it is the bump behind the tree right at the horizon line.  Is that a rock or island?  Again, not much you could do because of the type of challenge.  But that is honestly about all I could find wrong with the shot. Love your profile shot, very cute.  And looking at your other pictures this was a very nice challenge for you!  You have a good eye for this and I can''t wait to see you rise in the ranks here. I hope my comments help and good luck in Future Challenges! Deannda', '2006-08-02 00:39:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2685957, 366212, 53147, '<td valign="top">Trading Post - A very pretty shot here. Nice colors in the sunset. The blues could have been saturated maybe a bit more but overall nice colors. I think if you had gotten a bit lower when taking the pic you may have gotten a better silhouette of the mom. The girl is nice against the water but the mom is kind of hidden a bit much in the sand and the surf. Overall good shot and it looks like you caight the sunset at the right time.</td>', 'Trading Post - A very pretty shot here. Nice colors in the sunset. The blues could have been saturated maybe a bit more but overall nice colors. I think if you had gotten a bit lower when taking the pic you may have gotten a better silhouette of the mom. The girl is nice against the water but the mom is kind of hidden a bit much in the sand and the surf. Overall good shot and it looks like you caight the sunset at the right time.', '2006-08-02 00:57:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2689646, 365829, 45651, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 7 as stated before maybe ohters would like more DOF.</td>', 'I gave this a 7 as stated before maybe ohters would like more DOF.', '2006-08-02 19:40:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2689961, 365370, 36371, '<td valign="top">7 yrs old eh? How old is the post processor? Really cool picture, tho.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-08-03 01:34:11.</i></td>', '7 yrs old eh? How old is the post processor? Really cool picture, tho.', '2006-08-02 21:56:44.000000', '2006-08-03 02:34:11.000000', 0),
(2692135, 364293, 53147, '<td valign="top">Trading Post - Good overall shot here. Simple and clean composition, good lighting on the boy and nice subdued colors. There doesnt really seem to be anything that I can point out that hurt you here outside of maybe just not alot of "wow" interest in it. But you did capture what your title suggests and you caught it well.</td>', 'Trading Post - Good overall shot here. Simple and clean composition, good lighting on the boy and nice subdued colors. There doesnt really seem to be anything that I can point out that hurt you here outside of maybe just not alot of "wow" interest in it. But you did capture what your title suggests and you caught it well.', '2006-08-03 13:07:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2692196, 364737, 40355, '<td valign="top">I can see the cloud ship, no problem.  I agree with the previous comment that a bit more beach would have grounded it better for the challenge, but it''s a fun shot and well done.</td>', 'I can see the cloud ship, no problem.  I agree with the previous comment that a bit more beach would have grounded it better for the challenge, but it''s a fun shot and well done.', '2006-08-03 13:26:58.000000', NULL, 0),
