(3162571, 364100, 46314, '<td valign="top">I like this photo. Although I think the tones are a bit dull, and the image could have been a lot sharper - hyperfocal depth of field and sharp focus would have helped.<br/> <br/>However, I really like how the leading line of the shore pulls your eye up through the dots of colour on the beach around the coastline. Also the dots of colour on the beach offset nicely against the bands of colour running down vertically (grass, sand, sea).<br/> <br/>And I don''t have a problem with the shoreline in the middle of the pic. The bands of sea colour are nicely balanced by the band of land colour. And the dots of people on the beach are balanced by the bathers in the water.<br/> <br/>Maybe that centred composition wouldn''t have looked as odd if the sky had been cropped away, and all that was left was the sea separated from the beach...</td>', 'I like this photo. Although I think the tones are a bit dull, and the image could have been a lot sharper - hyperfocal depth of field and sharp focus would have helped. However, I really like how the leading line of the shore pulls your eye up through the dots of colour on the beach around the coastline. Also the dots of colour on the beach offset nicely against the bands of colour running down vertically (grass, sand, sea). And I don''t have a problem with the shoreline in the middle of the pic. The bands of sea colour are nicely balanced by the band of land colour. And the dots of people on the beach are balanced by the bathers in the water. Maybe that centred composition wouldn''t have looked as odd if the sky had been cropped away, and all that was left was the sea separated from the beach...', '2006-12-30 16:45:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(3197379, 366078, 46177, '<td valign="top">I think this is a very beautiful shot, don''t know how you could improve on it.</td>', 'I think this is a very beautiful shot, don''t know how you could improve on it.', '2007-01-08 18:46:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(3197387, 366078, 69350, '<td valign="top">I wasn''t a member yet when this challenge came out. I will definitely give this a 10. I like negative space so the lack of clouds doesn''t bother me.</td>', 'I wasn''t a member yet when this challenge came out. I will definitely give this a 10. I like negative space so the lack of clouds doesn''t bother me.', '2007-01-08 18:47:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(3197474, 366078, 20462, '<td valign="top">this is quality...good post..</td>', 'this is quality...good post..', '2007-01-08 19:03:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(3197756, 366078, 39429, '<td valign="top">I think your sky gives a feeling of being flatter than the image really is.  The other thing that happens with the sky is the horizontal split dividing the picture in half.  That "Rule of 1/3s" is not used here.  On DPC, using a 1/2 split instead of a 1/3 compostion can make the difference in several tenths of a point.<br/> <br/>So, in answer to your question of, "How could I have gotten a higher score?" you might have garnered a few tenths with a crop taking "a bit off the top."</td>', 'I think your sky gives a feeling of being flatter than the image really is.  The other thing that happens with the sky is the horizontal split dividing the picture in half.  That "Rule of 1/3s" is not used here.  On DPC, using a 1/2 split instead of a 1/3 compostion can make the difference in several tenths of a point. So, in answer to your question of, "How could I have gotten a higher score?" you might have garnered a few tenths with a crop taking "a bit off the top."', '2007-01-08 20:19:52.000000', NULL, 0),
